  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is an N-methyl morphinan-6-one with 3-methoxy and 14-hydroxy substitution; samidorphan, the closest supplied morphinan sharing the 6-keto/14-hydroxy core, has absolute oral bioavailability of 68.6–69% in healthy volunteers after oral dosing, directly supporting F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C03","C07","C14","C19","C33","C44"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Pethidine/meperidine, an opioid analgesic, has normal oral F of about 0.48 and cirrhotic F of 0.80–0.87; all reported values exceed the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C11","C18","C20","C43","C49","C50","C51"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for related morphinans (morphine, hydromorphone metabolite, naltrexone) show measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing, consistent with oral absorption; none provides an affirmative F < 20% result for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C97","C65","C98","C99","C87","C78","C83","C58","C95","C56","C55","C84","C68","C79"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Pentazocine and meptazinol high-F values are cirrhosis-dependent (control F 0.18 and ~4-fold lower than cirrhotic 27.9%, respectively); these contexts are not transferable to the no-condition query and do not affirm F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C47","C29","C48"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C97","C65","C98","C99","C87","C78","C83","C58","C95","C56","C55","C84","C68","C79"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule itself is present in the supplied records.",
    "L3 records are mostly single-arm oral AUC/Cmax without IV comparator; they cannot establish absolute F for the query or related molecules.",
    "Most high-F opioid records are from cirrhotic patients; healthy-control values for pentazocine and meptazinol are lower, limiting transferability to the no-condition query.",
    "No formulation, dose, prandial state, or species data are supplied for the query.",
    "The query's 3-methoxy substitution differs from samidorphan's 3-carboxamide/4-hydroxy and from naltrexone/naloxone 3-OH; effects on first-pass metabolism are not directly measured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high. The query is an N-methyl morphinan-6-one (oxycodone core); the closest supplied morphinan analog samidorphan has absolute oral F of 68.6–69% in healthy volunteers, and pethidine normal F (~0.48) also exceeds threshold. L3 oral exposure records for related morphinans show measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing and provide no affirmative F < 20% evidence. No contradictory threshold-relevant evidence appears; confidence remains high."
}

